Closes #27836

`to_primitive` gave `Undetermined` for a sequence ending in an array or object literal, so constant evaluation of `+` took the numeric path (it only needs one operand to be numeric), and `evaluate_value_to_number`, which does look through the sequence, turned `[]` into `0`:

```js
const u = true + (globalThis.x, []);
console.log(u);
// before: !0+(globalThis.x,[]),console.log(1);       -> 1
// after:  !0+(globalThis.x,[]),console.log(`true`);  -> true
```

`to_primitive` now uses the last expression of a sequence, as `value_type` and `to_boolean` already do. Added `test_fold_add_sequence_ending_in_object`, which fails without the fix. No snapshot changes.

Found with a differential fuzzer. Written with AI assistance; verified with `cargo test`, `clippy`, `fmt --check`, `minsize`, `allocs` and `coverage -- minifier`. I reviewed the diff.

