Fixes #27808

When a ternary, `if` or `switch` inside `try` picks a value based on a prop, the compiler treated that value as a constant, so anything built from it was cached once per mount.

```jsx
function Component({ cond }) {
  let value;
  try {
    if (cond) {
      value = "a";
    } else {
      value = "b";
    }
  } catch {
    value = "c";
  }
  return <div>{value}</div>;
}
```

```diff
-  if ($[0] === Symbol.for("react.memo_cache_sentinel")) {
+  if ($[0] !== value) {
     t1 = <div>{value}</div>;
```

Before this PR, changing `cond` from `true` to `false` still rendered `a`.

## Cause

Inside `try`, every assignment ends its block with a "may throw" edge to the `catch`. When `infer_reactive_places` looked for the branch that decides a value, it stopped at that edge and never reached `if (cond)`.

The same logic in Babel's React Compiler (facebook/react main, `098d2e87`):

- [`HIRBuilder.push`](compiler/packages/babel-plugin-react-compiler/src/HIR/HIRBuilder.ts#L164-L181) ends the block after each instruction in `try` with a `maybe-throw` edge to the handler.
- [`instructionMayThrow`](compiler/packages/babel-plugin-react-compiler/src/Optimization/PruneMaybeThrows.ts#L96-L107) keeps that edge for every store.
- [`InferReactivePlaces`](compiler/packages/babel-plugin-react-compiler/src/Inference/InferReactivePlaces.ts#L235-L242) marks a phi with constant operands reactive only if a predecessor is controlled by a reactive branch.
